@startuml

title A report instance, from admission to a terminal state

hide empty description

state "admission" as adm <<choice>>
[*] --> adm : trigger (one per firing id)
adm --> skipped : the concurrency policy is skip\nand a run is in flight
adm --> failed : the concurrency policy is fail\nand a run is in flight
adm --> queued : a run is in flight under the queue policy,\nor the tenant or party quota is full
adm --> pending : admitted

queued --> pending : promotion\n(oldest of the tenant whose party\nis under its quota)
queued --> cancelled : a person cancels
pending --> running : the first step is dispatched
pending --> failed : the start is refused
running --> completed : finalise
running --> failed : a step fails, a deadline expires,\nor the grant lapses
running --> cancelled : a person cancels

completed --> [*]
failed --> [*]
skipped --> [*]
cancelled --> [*]

note right of queued
  Every terminal transition of a tenant's run
  promotes at most one queued run of that tenant.
  A sweep each minute promotes runs that an
  event missed.
end note

@enduml
